{
  "Small badge beside the product name; labels this page as an interactive demo/sandbox, not a children's playground\u0004playground": "playground",
  "Tooltip on a status dot. 'isReady()' is an API name — keep it verbatim. 'gate UI on this' = show the UI only once it is ready; 'flash-of-untranslated-content' is the technical term for untranslated text briefly showing (FOUC)\u0004isReady() — gate UI on this to avoid flash-of-untranslated-content": "isReady() — gate UI on this to avoid flash-of-untranslated-content",
  "ready": "ready",
  "loading…": "loading…",
  "Heading above the sidebar table-of-contents navigation links\u0004On this page": "On this page",
  "Hero tagline (marketing register). 'Angular' is the framework name and 'i18n' the abbreviation for internationalization — keep both. 'signal-first' means built around Angular Signals; render the technical sense, not 'first signal'\u0004Angular i18n, the signal-first way": "Angular i18n, the signal-first way",
  "Hero subheading (marketing prose). Keep the product/tech names verbatim: 'ng-linguo', 'Angular', 'SignalStore', 'HTML'. 'signals'/'store methods' are Angular Signals concepts; 'reads'/'writes' are data access, not literal reading/writing\u0004ng-linguo is a complete internationalization solution for Angular built on a SignalStore. Reads are signals, writes are store methods, and translators never see a line of HTML. Flip the language switcher above and watch every example below re-render reactively.": "ng-linguo is a complete internationalization solution for Angular built on a SignalStore. Reads are signals, writes are store methods, and translators never see a line of HTML. Flip the language switcher above and watch every example below re-render reactively.",
  "Section heading: initial setup / installation of the library\u0004Setup": "Setup",
  "Card title. 'store' = the ng-linguo SignalStore (a noun); 'Bootstrap' = set up / initialize\u0004Bootstrap the store": "Bootstrap the store",
  "Card body (developer-docs tone). Keep API names verbatim: provideTranslate(), restoreLang(). 'store' = the SignalStore; 'loads' = fetches translations; 'Dictionaries' = the JSON translation files; 'keyed by source string' = the English text is the lookup key\u0004provideTranslate() wires up the store; it never loads automatically — restoreLang() is the explicit kick-off. Dictionaries are plain JSON keyed by source string.": "provideTranslate() wires up the store; it never loads automatically — restoreLang() is the explicit kick-off. Dictionaries are plain JSON keyed by source string.",
  "Section heading. 'pipe' is the Angular template-pipe concept — keep the technical term; [code] wraps the code symbol 't'\u0004The [code]t[/code] pipe": "The [code]t[/code] pipe",
  "Card title. 'template' = the Angular HTML template\u0004Translate in the template": "Translate in the template",
  "Card body. 'key' = the lookup key; 'falls through to the source' = shows the original English when no translation exists; 'blank' = empty\u0004The source English string is the key. With no translation it falls through to the source, so the UI is never blank.": "The source English string is the key. With no translation it falls through to the source, so the UI is never blank.",
  "He was driving incredibly fast!": "He was driving incredibly fast!",
  "Section heading. 'directive' is the Angular directive concept — keep the technical term; [code] wraps the code symbol '[t]'\u0004The [code][[t][/code] directive": "The [code][[t][/code] directive",
  "Card title. 'element' = an HTML / DOM element\u0004Translate an element": "Translate an element",
  "Card body. 'signals' = Angular Signals; 'dictionary' = the JSON translation file; 'directive' = the Angular [t] directive; 'subscription bookkeeping' = manually managing RxJS subscriptions\u0004Reads through to the store's signals — once a dictionary loads, the directive re-renders with no subscription bookkeeping.": "Reads through to the store's signals — once a dictionary loads, the directive re-renders with no subscription bookkeeping.",
  "Card title. 'TypeScript' is the programming language name — keep verbatim\u0004Translate in TypeScript": "Translate in TypeScript",
  "Card body. 'the pipe' = the Angular t pipe; 'component code' = TypeScript class code; keep computed() verbatim; 'params' = the ICU parameters; 'reactive' = updates automatically\u0004The pipe's counterpart for component code. Read it inside a computed() and it stays reactive to both params and the active language.": "The pipe's counterpart for component code. Read it inside a computed() and it stays reactive to both params and the active language.",
  "Section heading: grammatical plural forms (one file / many files)\u0004Plurals": "Plurals",
  "Card title. 'Cardinal plurals' = counting forms (1 file / 2 files), as opposed to ordinals\u0004Cardinal plurals across languages": "Cardinal plurals across languages",
  "Card body. EN/PL = English/Polish; one/few/many/other are CLDR plural-category names — keep them in English; 'count' is a variable name (keep); 'category switch' = the plural form changing\u0004EN has one/other; PL has one/few/many/other; an exact 0 variant reads better than '0'. Walk count through 1, 2, 5, 22 in Polish to see the category switch.": "EN has one/other; PL has one/few/many/other; an exact 0 variant reads better than '0'. Walk count through 1, 2, 5, 22 in Polish to see the category switch.",
  "Section heading: ordinal numbers (1st, 2nd, 3rd …), not cardinal counts\u0004Ordinals": "Ordinals",
  "Card title. 'Ordinal' = ranking forms (1st/2nd/3rd); 'categories' = the CLDR plural categories\u0004Ordinal categories": "Ordinal categories",
  "Card body. st/nd/rd/th are the English ordinal suffixes; one/two/few/other are CLDR category names (keep in English); EN/PL/DE = English/Polish/German; '{n}.' shows the number followed by a period\u0004EN uses st/nd/rd/th (one/two/few/other); PL and DE collapse to a plain '{n}.'.": "EN uses st/nd/rd/th (one/two/few/other); PL and DE collapse to a plain '{n}.'.",
  "Section heading. 'select' is the ICU MessageFormat 'select' construct (pick a variant by gender) — not a dropdown and not the verb 'to select'\u0004Gender select": "Gender select",
  "Card title. 'Select' = the ICU select construct (choose a variant by value), not a dropdown; 'a string' = a text value\u0004Select on a string": "Select on a string",
  "Card body. 'pronoun' = he/she/they; 'gendered past-tense verb' = a verb form that changes with gender (as in Polish); 'count × gender' = the combination of both; 'cross-product' = every combination\u0004EN swaps the pronoun; PL swaps the gendered past-tense verb. The second line combines count × gender — a cross-product that differs per language.": "EN swaps the pronoun; PL swaps the gendered past-tense verb. The second line combines count × gender — a cross-product that differs per language.",
  "Section heading: locale-aware number formatting (digit-group separators)\u0004Number formatting": "Number formatting",
  "Card title. 'grouping' = digit-group separators in numbers (1,000 vs 1.000 vs 1 000); 'Locale-aware' = follows the active language\u0004Locale-aware grouping": "Locale-aware grouping",
  "Card body. ':number' is an ICU formatter token (keep verbatim); en/de/pl = English/German/Polish; the figures show how each locale groups digits\u0004The :number formatter follows the active locale: en 1,234,567 · de 1.234.567 · pl 1 234 567.": "The :number formatter follows the active locale: en 1,234,567 · de 1.234.567 · pl 1 234 567.",
  "Section heading. 'Context' = the translation disambiguation feature (gettext msgctxt); 'homonyms' = words spelled the same but meaning different things\u0004Context (homonyms)": "Context (homonyms)",
  "Card title about homonyms / disambiguation\u0004Same word, different meaning": "Same word, different meaning",
  "Card body. 'context' is the ng-linguo option name (keep verbatim); 'key' = lookup key; 'gettext msgctxt' is a technical term (keep); 'note for translators' = a hint; 'sense' = meaning\u0004context is part of the key (gettext msgctxt) and doubles as a note for translators. Switch to Polish to see each sense diverge.": "context is part of the key (gettext msgctxt) and doubles as a note for translators. Switch to Polish to see each sense diverge.",
