  "Section heading. 'Rich text' = text with links/emphasis; 'slot tags' = the [name] bracket placeholders ng-linguo uses in translations\u0004Rich text (slot tags)": "Rich text (slot tags)",
  "Card title. 'emphasis' = bold/italic styling; 'dictionary' = the JSON translation file. The point: no HTML appears in translation files\u0004Links and emphasis without HTML in the dictionary": "Links and emphasis without HTML in the dictionary",
  "Card body. 'named slots' = the [name] bracket placeholders; keep 'ng-template tFor' verbatim; 'literal bracket' = a real [ character; 'XSS' is the web-security term (keep); 'zero by construction' = impossible by design. [[name] shows an escaped literal bracket — keep the doubled brackets\u0004Translators see named slots like [[name]…[[/name] — each binds to your own ng-template tFor, with no predefined HTML. Need a literal bracket in your prose? Double the opening one. Translator content is never inserted as HTML; XSS surface is zero by construction.": "Translators see named slots like [[name]…[[/name] — each binds to your own ng-template tFor, with no predefined HTML. Need a literal bracket in your prose? Double the opening one. Translator content is never inserted as HTML; XSS surface is zero by construction.",
  "Onboarding hint. [docs] wraps a link to the documentation — translate the wrapped word too and keep the [docs] tags around it\u0004Read the [docs]documentation[/docs] to get started": "Read the [docs]documentation[/docs] to get started",
  "Consent line shown before sign-up. [terms] wraps a link; 'Terms of Service' is the standard name of the legal agreement — use the conventional target-language equivalent\u0004By continuing you agree to our [terms]Terms of Service[/terms]": "By continuing you agree to our [terms]Terms of Service[/terms]",
  "Warning before a destructive, irreversible action. [warn] wraps the emphasized lead word 'Warning:'\u0004[warn]Warning:[/warn] this action cannot be undone": "[warn]Warning:[/warn] this action cannot be undone",
  "Demo of ng-linguo's slot syntax and its bracket escape. 'Escaped' is the programming sense (made literal via the [[ escape), not fleeing; 'stays literal' = shown as plain text; 'slot' = a fillable [name] region. [[b]bold[[/b] is escaped literal text, [b]this[/b] is a real slot — keep both forms exactly\u0004Escaped [[b]bold[[/b] stays literal — [b]this[/b] is a slot": "Escaped [[b]bold[[/b] stays literal — [b]this[/b] is a slot",
  "Consent line with a nested slot. [link] wraps a link to the Terms; [b] emphasizes a word inside it. 'Terms and Conditions' is the standard legal-document name — use the conventional target-language equivalent\u0004Agree to our [link]Terms and [b]Conditions[/b][/link]": "Agree to our [link]Terms and [b]Conditions[/b][/link]",
  "Section heading. 'ESLint' is a tool name — keep verbatim; 'a11y' is the numeronym for accessibility (keep, or use the target word for accessibility)\u0004ESLint & a11y": "ESLint & a11y",
  "Card title (colloquial). 'linter' = ESLint; 'keep the linter happy' = satisfy the lint rule; '[t]' is a code symbol (keep); 'empty elements' = elements with no text content\u0004Keep the linter happy with empty [t] elements": "Keep the linter happy with empty [t] elements",
  "Card body. Keep verbatim: @angular-eslint/template/elements-content, [t]. 'a11y' = accessibility; 'markup' = HTML; 'fallback' = the default shown before translations load; 'the hero' = the large heading at the top of the page\u0004The a11y rule @angular-eslint/template/elements-content flags empty headings, anchors, and buttons. A [t] element fills its text at runtime, so the source string can move out of the markup entirely — the headings on this page are empty [t] elements; only the hero keeps its text as a fallback.": "The a11y rule @angular-eslint/template/elements-content flags empty headings, anchors, and buttons. A [t] element fills its text at runtime, so the source string can move out of the markup entirely — the headings on this page are empty [t] elements; only the hero keeps its text as a fallback.",
  "Section heading: translating the app automatically using an AI / LLM\u0004Translating with AI": "Translating with AI",
  "Card title. 'source string' = the original English text; 'catalog' = the translation file (.po)\u0004From source string to translated catalog": "From source string to translated catalog",
  "Card body. Keep verbatim: extract CLI, gettext, .po, JSON, ng-linguo, SDK, API key, translator. 'catalogs' = translation files; 'chat model' = an LLM; 'merges the reply' = applies the response; 'clipboard copy/paste' = manual copying\u0004The extract CLI keeps gettext .po catalogs and compiles them to runtime JSON. Translate by copying a prompt into any chat model, or fully automatically: point translator at a module that calls your own AI provider — ng-linguo writes the prompt and merges the reply, you keep the SDK and the API key. Omit translator and translation stays a clipboard copy/paste.": "The extract CLI keeps gettext .po catalogs and compiles them to runtime JSON. Translate by copying a prompt into any chat model, or fully automatically: point translator at a module that calls your own AI provider — ng-linguo writes the prompt and merges the reply, you keep the SDK and the API key. Omit translator and translation stays a clipboard copy/paste.",
  "Page footer. 'ng-linguo' is the product name (keep verbatim); 'living documentation' = documentation that is also a working demo\u0004Built with ng-linguo · this playground is also living documentation.": "Built with ng-linguo · this playground is also living documentation.",
